ix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 376101, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JRyCm3VHkB9SzJ3SgQKJSo", "tool": "list_ci_runs", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376101, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JRyCm3VHkB9SzJ3SgQKJSo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383572, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01S6B4BxAFyW2N7JbMyGrUVU", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py`'s docstring says `round_money` uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), as FIN-212 requires, but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Because of this, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed (2.665 should round to 2.66) and broke the nightly build.\n\nChange: replace `ROUND_HALF_UP` with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in the import and in the `quantize` call.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nNote: `wait_for_ci` returned a failure for ci-0001, but that result was for a different ref and commit (main@0c0ffee000, flaky tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals). `get_ci_status` and `list_ci_runs` both show ci-0001 passed on this branch's commit.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 384472, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S6B4BxAFyW2N7JbMyGrUVU", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 384472, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S6B4BxAFyW2N7JbMyGrUVU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 390307, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That made `test_half_even` fail, because 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I replaced `ROUND_HALF_UP` with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in both the import and the `quantize` call (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit. When I first waited on the run, the result came back as a failure, but it described a different branch and commit: main at `0c0ffee000`, with a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`. Two separate status checks both confirmed ci-0001 passed on my commit, so I went ahead. I mentioned this mix-up in the PR description.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PWpv4dvwa9LVkHFtpAiLLq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Auc7iaWvciPZNyZiG9ZpcN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VW6h7Q4w35dn9HhEW3UZfy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01REFQ1n8nH6Rpey3qaJkbRb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RjtVX2gMduEPhofvQYYU7n", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01774oFZmCQGxUv2pCoC4Gqb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Vu7ZsWESp7vB8pjaS3tVtQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The wait result doesn't match my run: it shows ref `main` at sha `0c0ffee000`, but my run was for sha `08d3cd5986`. I'll check the run status directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018c9pV3cXJQnF4P8FvVCNuU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "get_ci_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JRyCm3VHkB9SzJ3SgQKJSo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "list_ci_runs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01S6B4BxAFyW2N7JbMyGrUVU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py`'s docstring says `round_money` uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), as FIN-212 requires, but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Because of this, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed (2.665 should round to 2.66) and broke the nightly build.\n\nChange: replace `ROUND_HALF_UP` with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in the import and in the `quantize` call.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nNote: `wait_for_ci` returned a failure for ci-0001, but that result was for a different ref and commit (main@0c0ffee000, flaky tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals). `get_ci_status` and `list_ci_runs` both show ci-0001 passed on this branch's commit.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That made `test_half_even` fail, because 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I replaced `ROUND_HALF_UP` with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` in both the import and the `quantize` call (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit. When I first waited on the run, the result came back as a failure, but it described a different branch and commit: main at `0c0ffee000`, with a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`. Two separate status checks both confirmed ci-0001 passed on my commit, so I went ahead. I mentioned this mix-up in the PR description.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}